This crate is an original implementation for nv-rs of the role ShowOff xNVSE plays for mods
(ADR-0016's "later built-ins"). It contains no code of the plugin and no decompiled code, and
none was read for it: it is written from public behaviour and documentation only.

Plugin: ShowOff xNVSE, release 1.84 is the target (the owner's list had 1.83). Opcode block
0x3c93. DLL file name ShowOffNVSE.dll as seen in the owner's installation. Nexus mod 72541.

Sources used (2026-11-14): none beyond xNVSE's documented plugin interface. Its Nexus page and
GECK Wiki category were not read (bot blocks answer HTTP 403; no workaround was attempted).

Sources used (2026-11-20): the plugin's public repository (github.com/Demorome/ShowOff-NVSE, which
states no licence) for four facts only, all from the registration list in ShowOffNVSE.cpp: the
name the plugin hands xNVSE (`ShowOffNVSE Plugin`), its version number (184), the opcode the
list gives GetActorHasBaseFlag (0x3CE0) and the opcode slots the list registers (0x3C93 to
0x3D69, 215). No function body was read and no code is copied.

Licence check: the repository states none, so this crate takes nothing but facts (names, opcodes,
version, behaviour as publicly documented) and builds a command only from its public name and
parameters and from how scripts call it.

Commands (2026-11-20): ActorHasBaseFlag (long name GetActorHasBaseFlag) is built from its public
name and one integer parameter, how Tale of Two Wastelands' scripts call it (`ref.ActorHasBaseFlag 5`,
in conditions of trap scripts, and its opcode 0x3CE0 read from those scripts' compiled form) and the
engine's own actor base layout (the flags word of TESActorBaseData). It answers 1 when that bit of
the actor base's flags is set, 0 otherwise.
